3. Common Variant Association Analysis

Single-variant association analyses were performed using REGENIE Step 2.

#Binary Phenotype Analysis. Used for dichotomous traits such as disease status.
regenie --step 2 --bed input_prefix --phenoFile phenotype_file.txt --phenoCol phenotype --covarFile covariates_file.txt --covarCol covariate1,covariate2,covariate3 --bt --firth \
--ignore-pred --bsize 1000 --htp phenotype --out output_prefix

#Quantitative Phenotype Analysis. Used for continuous quantitative traits.
regenie --step 2 --bed input_prefix --phenoFile phenotype_file.txt --phenoCol quantitative_trait --covarFile covariates_file.txt --covarCol covariate1,covariate2 --qt \
--ignore-pred --bsize 1000 --htp quantitative_trait --out output_prefix

#Quantitative Phenotype Analysis with Sample Exclusion. Used when treated individuals or specific samples needed to be excluded.
regenie --step 2 --bed input_prefix --phenoFile phenotype_file.txt --phenoCol quantitative_trait --covarFile covariates_file.txt --covarCol covariate1,covariate2,covariate3 --qt \
--ignore-pred --remove samples_to_exclude.txt --bsize 1000 --htp quantitative_trait --out output_prefix

Description of Parameters
--step 2	Performs REGENIE Step 2 association testing.
--bed	Prefix of PLINK binary genotype files.
--phenoFile	Phenotype file.
--phenoCol	Phenotype column to analyze.
--covarFile	Covariate file.
--covarCol	Covariates included in the model.
--bt	Binary trait analysis.
--qt  Quantitative trait analysis using linear regression.
--firth	Applies Firth logistic regression correction.
--ignore-pred	Runs the analysis without LOCO predictions.
--remove  Removes samples listed in the specified file before association testing.
--bsize	Block size.
--htp	Phenotype label used in outputs.
--out	Prefix for output files.

